    "notes": "Aranese accentuation follows the Conselh Generau d'Aran norm, which is the classical-norm system: a word ending in a vowel or in a vowel + -s is paroxytone, anything else is oxytone, and a written accent always wins. Infinitives are OXYTONE (-ar -er -ir), so those endings are NOT paroxytone triggers; the final -r is itself silent. Unstressed ⟨a⟩ is [ɑ~ɔ] and phrase-final ⟨a⟩ is [ɔ], while STRESSED ⟨a⟩ stays [a] (Wikipedia, Aranese dialect, vowel table).",
